From 36687c12161f14fb0616938046b7e5e8a882d663 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Victoren <151829597+0xvictoren@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 15:30:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix CCTP bridge stalling on challenges stuck at PENDING

A UCW challenge only flips to COMPLETE once Circle has finished processing
it end to end. For CONTRACT_EXECUTION challenges (approve, depositForBurn)
that happens after the user's PIN and often after the transaction is already
mined, so polling the challenge status alone reports PENDING for a burn that
is irreversibly on-chain. The app treated that as a terminal failure, so
attestation and mint never started for burns that had actually succeeded.

Server:
- classifyChallenge/readChallengeSettlement decide from the challenge status
  AND the correlated transaction; a challenge whose tx has a hash is settled
  even while its own status still reads PENDING.
- waitForChallengesComplete reports settled/dead per challenge plus the first
  observed tx hash, and no longer re-reads challenges that already settled.
- Raise verify windows to match Circle's own 10-minute strategy default
  instead of cutting healthy burns off at 60s.
- Supply resolveTypedDataSignature to the UCW adapter. Without it the
  strategy does not advertise the evm-typed-data family, so App Kit silently
  drops to another route or stalls. Signatures reach the server through a new
  POST /v1/app-kit/jobs/:id/signature relay, since a typed-data signature is
  delivered only to the client that executed the challenge.

Client:
- Do not abandon a bridge when the burn challenge cannot be confirmed. Only a
  user cancel or a FAILED/EXPIRED challenge stops the pipeline; otherwise fall
  through to /cctp/finish, which resolves the hash and drives attest + mint.
- Never discard the activity for an inconclusive burn, and never re-prompt for
  a challenge that has already settled.
- challenge.html waits for a terminal SDK callback instead of resolving on
  IN_PROGRESS, and the challenge screen lets the SDK flush before unmounting
  the WebView. Tearing the iframe down mid-flush left challenges at PENDING.
- Capture and relay typed-data signatures from the W3S SDK result.

Adds unit tests for the settlement rule.
